{"annotations":{"destructiveHint":false,"idempotentHint":true,"openWorldHint":true,"readOnlyHint":true},"description":"Get one style's profile and, optionally, its design tokens, one component recipe, and the full implementation brief. Everything ships through this single tool so the server stays small: pass include: [\"tokens\"], [\"recipe\"], [\"brief\"] or a combination.\n\nStyle data is read from the live catalogue with a five-minute cache; when live data is unavailable, a bundled snapshot may be returned and marked with origin and fallbackReason.\n\nArgs:\n  - slug (string): style identifier, e.g. \"glassmorphism\", \"neo-brutalist\".\n  - include (array, optional): sections to attach \u2014 \"tokens\", \"recipe\", \"brief\".\n  - component (string, optional): recipe id for include: [\"recipe\"], e.g. \"button\"; defaults to the style's first recipe.\n\nReturns JSON: { slug, name, nameEn, category, tags, description, philosophy, colors, doList, dontList, keywords, hasTokens, hasRecipes, recipeIds, shadcnInstall, url, quality, origin, fallbackReason?, tokens?, recipe?, brief? }.\n\nExamples:\n  - \"how should I use neo-brutalist?\" -> slug: \"neo-brutalist\"\n  - \"give me the glassmorphism button code\" -> slug: \"glassmorphism\", include: [\"recipe\"], component: \"button\"\n  - Returns an error with a hint if the slug is unknown.","execution":{"taskSupport":"forbidden"},"inputSchema":{"$schema":"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#","additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"component":{"description":"Recipe id when include contains 'recipe'; defaults to the first recipe","minLength":1,"type":"string"},"include":{"description":"Sections to attach: \"tokens\", \"recipe\", \"brief\"","items":{"enum":["tokens","recipe","brief"],"type":"string"},"type":"array"},"slug":{"description":"Style slug, e.g. 'glassmorphism'","minLength":1,"type":"string"}},"required":["slug"],"type":"object"},"name":"stylekit_get_style","outputSchema":{"$schema":"http://json-schema.o